        "original_id": "3786d69f-3289-51b9-9d2f-6d3c84c3820a",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Rosary Church\n- Concepts: Basilica, Gothic style, Roman Basilican model, church architecture\n\nFacts:\n- A basilica is a type of building, usually a Christian church, that is typically rectangular with a central nave and aisles, a slightly raised platform, and an apse at one or both ends.\n- In Europe and the Americas, the basilica plan has been the most common architectural style for churches, though it has become less dominant in new buildings since the later 20th century.\n- Today, the term basilica is often used for any large, ornate church building, especially in Roman Catholic and Eastern Orthodox contexts, even when the building does not strictly follow the basilica plan.\n- Rosary Church is in Gothic style, and its original plan was based on a Roman Basilican model.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
