        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "45ec3f70-f13f-5e2c-8ec4-f88b067f7143",
        "text": "Page: Rosary Church. Sentence: The church is in Gothic style; the original plan was based on a Roman Basilican model.\nPage: Basilica. Sentence: A basilica is a type of building, usually a Christian church, that is typically rectangular with a central nave and aisles, usually with a slightly raised platform and an apse at one or both ends.\nPage: Basilica. Sentence: In Europe and the Americas it is the most common architectural style for churches though this building plan has become less dominant in new buildings since the later 20th century.\nPage: Basilica. Sentence: Today the term \"basilica\" is often used to refer to any large, ornate church building, especially Roman Catholic and Eastern Orthodox, even if it does not strictly follow this style.",
